### R1-CORR-001 == SAFE-MAJ-003 (same defect, 2 lenses): prior_restore_evidence_present ignores REPO@BRANCH argument

**Bug:** scripts/enable-required-check.sh prior_restore_evidence_present takes target="${REPO}@${BRANCH}" as 2nd argument but the awk pattern matches any '**Restoring TO:**' line regardless of which repo's section header it belongs to. Uncommitted restore evidence on a DIFFERENT adopter fires the Gate-3-requirement guard against the current repo. Cross-target false positive.

**Fix (option b — keep cross-repo scope intentional, document it):** since the depth-defense gate-3 enforcement has been carved out to 024B-extras-2, this guard's primary purpose is reduced. In scripts/enable-required-check.sh:

1. Update the prior_restore_evidence_present function comment to: '# Checks for ANY uncommitted/working-tree restore evidence in the branch-protection-log.md — intentionally cross-repo scope. Used by the forward-mode warning that a pending restore commit may exist.'
2. Drop the `${REPO}@${BRANCH}` 2nd argument from both the function signature AND the single call site (line ~700-ish forward-mode-safety section). Function takes only $1=log_path.
3. Update the call site's diagnostic to: 'WARNING: uncommitted prior-restore evidence detected in branch-protection-log.md — commit or revert pending restore-mode entries before invoking forward mode.' Exit code stays the same.

This closes the false-positive surface by acknowledging the cross-repo scope is intentional in 024B-extras-1's contract. The repo-scoped variant is what 024B-extras-2 needs for Gate 3 enforcement.

