ck_invocation_log_entry.sh:3098:  \"required_signatures\": {\"enabled\": true}\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3103:  \"required_status_checks\": {\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3105:    \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3110:  \"required_signatures\": {\"enabled\": true}\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3149:  \"required_status_checks\": {\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3151:    \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3156:    \"required_signatures\": {\"enabled\": true}\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3196:  \"required_status_checks\": {\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3198:    \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3203:  \"required_signatures\": {\"enabled\": true}\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3208:  \"required_status_checks\": {\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3210:    \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3215:  \"required_signatures\": {\"enabled\": true}\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:88:| D-035 | 2026-04-30 | Adopt the WP-SCP-020 slice 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine. The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate). Adopters of the SCP federation primitive enable this required status check on their default branch via `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` from the SCP repo. The script applies branch protection in two API calls (unified PUT for status-checks/admins/reviews + dedicated POST to `required_signatures` sub-resource per the GitHub API shape), refuses to bypass admin enforcement without an explicit `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` acknowledgement flag, refuses to run in CI (CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true env-var guards), preserves any pre-existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it, and emits an invocation-log block (operator, timestamp, script SHA256 + git SHA, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON) for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure: an apply without the log entry is considered unrecorded. Estate cascade rollout (WP-SCP-024) drives this script across PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower; FLA pilot (WP-SCP-020.1) is the canary first invocation | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection), D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account), D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-status-check), D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection): every operational procedure that mutates third-party repository state ships an idempotent applier + ratifying D-NNN + invocation log convention. The bootstrap-only / no-CI guard reflects that this script writes to a third-party repo's branch protection — an automation tool that ran it unattended could mass-mutate the estate via stolen credentials before any operator noticed. The `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` confirmation reflects that `--no-enforce-admins` defeats the whole point of the federation primitive on the target repo and so should require explicit intent. The `required_pull_request_reviews` preservation reflects that adopters with multi-maintainer teams have legitimate review-shape state that 020G must not destroy. Identified at WP-SCP-020 §4 020G + 020G R1 review (3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 2 nit on safety, 2 MAJ + 4 MIN + nit on completeness, 3 MAJ + 2 MIN + 2 nit on correctness — fixpoint via fix-round-1) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:98:| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` and queries workflow-runs without a branch filter; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure with manual Gate 3 verification; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. The depth-defense surface (wrapper-SHA verification, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify) is carved into sibling slice 024B-extras-2 per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`; D-048 reserved for that slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:73:10. **No backwards-incompatible adopter-side work in cascade slices.** Each adopter's onboarding PR is purely additive (a new wrapper file + optional CODEOWNERS lines). Renames, deletions, or modifications to existing adopter-side files are out of scope. **If a conflict is discovered during cascade** (e.g. adopter has a stale `policy-check.yml` from a prior unrelated experiment): (a) the cascade slice CLOSES on the SCP side with status `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` (not deferred indefinitely); (b) a forward TF is filed (`TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>`) owned by the cascade slice author and targeting the adopter-side resolution (typically a rename); (c) when the conflict is resolved, a NEW cascade sub-slice opens for that adopter. This eliminates the open-ended \"defer\" state. Closes 024A R1 MIN-SAFE-006.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:171:- A `--restore <pre-state.json>` mode that consumes a captured before-state from a prior invocation log entry + reverses the branch-protection mutation (rollback path per invariant 7). Existing forward-mode behaviour unchanged.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:50:| **MINOR** (`v1.x.0`) | New `workflow_call` inputs (with safe defaults), new `SCP-R-NNN` rules added with `threshold: warn` baseline, new optional schema fields, new commit-status contexts (informational), new `disabled_rules:` reasons. | Recommended: review the release notes for new rules. None mandatory unless the adopter wants to opt into a new rule's `threshold: deny`. |\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:91:- Removing `--repo`, `--branch`, `--plan`, `--no-enforce-admins`, `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate`, `--restore`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions`, or `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flags from `scripts/enable-required-check.sh`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:109:- New commit-status contexts (the existing two are stable).\nSTATUS.md:40:- `required_status_checks: [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]` (strict).\nSTATUS.md:41:- `required_signatures: true` on every commit reaching `main`.\nSTATUS.md:55:| 1 | #53 | 020J | tag-protection + required_signatures applied |\nSTATUS.md:155:| 1 | Slice 024B-extras: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore` added with GET-shape → PUT-shape transform, posture-degradation acknowledgements, required-signatures sub-resource handling, and forward-mode safety checks (path-pinned workflow lookup, no branch filter on runs API, release-tag SHA validation, working-tree prior-entry detection). |\nSTATUS.md:317:- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (open): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence (docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md) — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7; merge-blocking AC for 024B-extras-1 per plan-doc §6 + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003; it does NOT cover Gate 3 wrapper-SHA verification, which moves to the `024B-extras-2` step-7 equivalent; closes when operator runs forward-mode + --restore round-trip on throw-away test repo + commits byte-for-byte match evidence.\nSTATUS.md:318:- **TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001** (open): Before 024C dispatch opens, operator must add `check-invocation-log-entry / check-invocation-log-entry` to main branch's `required_status_checks` list via `gh api -X PATCH repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/branches/main/protection` with the updated contexts list, then record the SCP-self REQCHECK enablement as a `STATUS.md` chain entry only. Do NOT modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; that log is reserved for adopter-side `enable-required-check.sh` invocations per D-035 scope. Without this step CI-enforcement is advisory only (the workflow runs but doesn't block merge). Close as part of 024C kickoff ceremony.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:859:5. Captures before-state, applies the unified PUT (status-checks + admins + reviews), then a separate POST to the `required_signatures` sub-resource.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:860:6. Verifies 4 properties (strict, contexts, enforce_admins, signatures) and emits the result.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:876:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:877:     --jq '{strict: .strict, contexts: .contexts}'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:878:   # expected (selectively): {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:881:2. Confirm `enforce_admins` and `required_signatures`:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:886:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_signatures --jq '.enabled'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:937:   # List current required-check contexts\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:938:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks --jq '.contexts'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:941:   Then PATCH the contexts list. **Important:** the PATCH replaces the contexts array entirely, it does not subtract. If `policy-check / scp/policy-check` is your only required check, pass an empty array; if you have other required checks, you MUST include them in the new array or this PATCH removes them too:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:945:   gh api -X PATCH repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:947:   {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": []}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:951:   gh api -X PATCH repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:953:   {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": [\"other-required-check-1\", \"other-required-check-2\"]}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:957:3. Optionally relax `enforce_admins` if it was set ONLY for the SCP gate. Keep `required_signatures` regardless — it is independent of SCP and a baseline supply-chain hygiene control.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1203:The `<pre-state.json>` input comes from the prior invocation log entry for the adopter repo and is the canonical pre-mutation state. The helper transforms the captured GET-shape JSON into the PUT-shape payload, strips envelope fields recursively, and restores `required_signatures` through its dedicated sub-resource. The rollback SLO is **less than 30 minutes** from operator decision to restored branch-protection state.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1211:- `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
